{title: Here Is Love}
{artist: William Rees & Robert Lowry}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 66}

Verse 1
[F]Here is love, vast [Bb]as the [F]ocean, [Dm]loving-[Bb]kindness [C]as the [F]flood,
when the Prince of [Bb]Life, our [F]ransom, [Dm]shed for [Bb]us his [C]precious [F]blood.
[C]Who his love will [F]not re[Bb]member? [F]Who can [Dm]cease to [C]sing his [F]praise?
He can never [Bb]be for[F]gotten [Dm]throughout [Bb]heaven's e[C]ternal [F]days.
